WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.464
Henry looked where Maggie was pointing.

2
00:00:16.465 --> 00:00:20.389
A teenage boy had just walked up behind the lemonade stand.

3
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:26.411
He was wearing jeans and a black T-shirt, and he had a tattoo of a snake on his arm.

4
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:29.478
"It's okay, Maggie," Henry said quickly.

5
00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:33.526
The teenager looked pretty tough, and Henry didn't want to cause trouble.

6
00:00:33.527 --> 00:00:36.365
"I'm sure he wasn't spying on us."

7
00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:39.233
Maggie frowned. "How do you know?

8
00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:45.445
Maybe he's building a float for the parade, and he was eavesdropping so he can steal our ideas."

9
00:00:45.446 --> 00:00:52.550
The teenager laughed. "Actually, my rock band is entering a float.

10
00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:55.609
But we're not doing any silly lemon stuff.

11
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.593
We're going to make our float look like a concert stage.

12
00:00:59.594 --> 00:01:04.398
Then we're going to play our music during the parade. It will be awesome!"

13
00:01:04.399 --> 00:01:07.481
"Do you live in Belltown?" Henry asked.

14
00:01:07.482 --> 00:01:11.304
"I moved here at the beginning of the summer," the teenager said.

15
00:01:11.305 --> 00:01:15.410
"My name is Stan, but everyone calls me Snake."

16
00:01:15.411 --> 00:01:22.022
"Welcome to Belltown, Snake." Cole poured a cup of lemonade.

17
00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:24.795
"Here's some lemonade—on the house."

18
00:01:24.796 --> 00:01:27.970
"Thanks." Snake drank the lemonade.

19
00:01:27.971 --> 00:01:31.374
"Maybe my band will stop by later to buy more.

20
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:34.386
We'll probably be thirsty after we practice.

21
00:01:34.387 --> 00:01:38.136
That reminds me—I have to go."

22
00:01:38.137 --> 00:01:41.172
Soon there were no customers in sight.

23
00:01:41.173 --> 00:01:46.602
"Hey, Nathan, can you watch the lemonade stand for a while?" Henry asked.

24
00:01:46.603 --> 00:01:51.460
"We should go work on our float. We only have two more days to finish it."

25
00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:54.233
"Yeah." Maggie picked up the laptop.

26
00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:57.767
"Plus, my mom doesn't know I have her computer."

27
00:01:57.768 --> 00:02:05.392
"Sure," Nathan said. "Have fun."

28
00:02:05.393 --> 00:02:08.948
The papier-mâché lemon was in Maggie's house.

29
00:02:08.949 --> 00:02:13.118
When it was finished, the kids were planning to attach it to a garden cart.

30
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:16.756
Maggie's father would pull the cart behind his lawn tractor.

31
00:02:16.757 --> 00:02:19.257
"It looks awesome," Cole said.

32
00:02:19.258 --> 00:02:22.790
"But we still need to attach Sherlock Holmes' hat."

33
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:27.684
Maggie dug into their craft supply box. "I think we're out of glue."

34
00:02:27.685 --> 00:02:34.223
"I'll go buy some," Henry offered. "You guys can keep working."

35
00:02:34.224 --> 00:02:37.016
Henry's house was right next door.

36
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:40.108
He grabbed his bike and rode toward Main Street.

37
00:02:40.109 --> 00:02:43.323
On the way there, he heard loud rock music.

38
00:02:43.324 --> 00:02:46.417
It was coming from the garage of a nearby house.

39
00:02:46.418 --> 00:02:50.801
The garage door was open, so Henry stopped and looked in.

40
00:02:50.802 --> 00:02:54.030
Four teenagers were inside playing instruments.

41
00:02:54.031 --> 00:02:59.913
One of the musicians was Snake. There were two other boys and a girl.

42
00:02:59.914 --> 00:03:02.574
Snake saw Henry looking in.

43
00:03:02.575 --> 00:03:06.470
He held up a hand, and the band stopped playing.

44
00:03:06.471 --> 00:03:09.332
The other three teens stared at Henry.

45
00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:13.330
Henry knew the drummer's name was Eddie and that this was his house.

46
00:03:13.331 --> 00:03:17.464
He also recognized the other two teens as students from the high school.

47
00:03:17.465 --> 00:03:20.005
But he didn't know any of them well.

48
00:03:20.006 --> 00:03:23.759
"Hey, it's the lemonade kid," Snake called with a smile.

49
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.646
"Did you bring us a drink?"

50
00:03:25.647 --> 00:03:29.957
"No," Henry said. "I like your music, though."

51
00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:35.105
"Cool," one of the other boys said with a grin. "You have good taste."

52
00:03:35.106 --> 00:03:39.445
Henry glanced at the girl. He was pretty sure her name was Jade.

53
00:03:39.446 --> 00:03:42.685
She was ignoring everyone else as she tuned her guitar.

54
00:03:42.686 --> 00:03:45.456
"Are you here to spy on us, Lemonade Kid?"

55
00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.807
Snake laughed and glanced at the others with a grin.

56
00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:51.499
"He and his friends are making a float too."

57
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:57.556
"Uh-oh," Eddie said. "So he's our competition for the prizes, huh?"

58
00:03:57.557 --> 00:04:00.111
"No way," the other boy said.

59
00:04:00.112 --> 00:04:03.740
"Our float is going to be awesome! We'll win for sure."

60
00:04:03.741 --> 00:04:06.692
Jade looked up from her guitar with a frown.

61
00:04:06.693 --> 00:04:12.300
"Can we get back to practicing?" she said. "I have to go to work soon."

62
00:04:12.301 --> 00:04:16.017
"Okay, okay." Snake strummed his bass guitar.

63
00:04:16.018 --> 00:04:19.028
"See you at the parade, Lemonade Kid."

64
00:04:19.029 --> 00:04:29.873
"See you." Henry hurried on as the music started again.

65
00:04:29.874 --> 00:04:33.692
"May I be excused, Mom?" Henry asked.

66
00:04:33.693 --> 00:04:37.369
It was the next day, and he'd just finished eating lunch.

67
00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.112
"Of course," his mother said. "Put your dishes in the sink.

68
00:04:42.113 --> 00:04:45.716
Are you going back to Maggie's house to work on your float?"

69
00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:48.765
Henry carried his plate and glass to the sink.

70
00:04:48.766 --> 00:04:52.275
"No, we worked on it all morning.

71
00:04:52.276 --> 00:04:57.411
I'm supposed to meet Maggie and Cole at the lemonade stand."

72
00:04:57.412 --> 00:05:01.166
When Henry reached the lemonade stand, his friends were already there.

73
00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.953
Maggie had her mother's laptop again.

74
00:05:03.954 --> 00:05:06.765
"What are you doing?" Henry asked her.

75
00:05:06.766 --> 00:05:11.586
"I want to leave a comment on the town website about our float," Maggie said.

76
00:05:11.587 --> 00:05:14.576
"Then people will look for us during the parade."

77
00:05:14.577 --> 00:05:18.352
"Are a lot of people leaving comments?" Cole asked.

78
00:05:18.353 --> 00:05:22.969
He and Henry watched as Maggie scrolled down to the comment section.

79
00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.246
Henry's eyes widened when he saw the latest comment.

80
00:05:26.247 --> 00:05:29.170
"Look at that!" he exclaimed.

81
00:05:29.171 --> 00:05:32.013
The comment was typed in capital letters.

82
00:05:32.014 --> 00:05:34.537
THE SUMMER PARADE IS FOR LOSERS.

83
00:05:34.538 --> 00:05:39.472
THE MAYOR SHOULD CANCEL IT—OR ELSE!
